{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>First occurrence</b><br>חמוקי. The knee-cap that is on the thigh, and some say it is like חמק (to pass), and its meaning is 'to walk.'" "חלאים. Round ornaments gathered together, like וחלי כתם." "אמן. A skilled craftsman, and in the sacred language it has no synonym." "<b>Second occurrence</b><br>He answered and said to her: 'How beautiful are your sandals,' and he called her 'daughter of a noble,' just as she said: 'the chariots of my noble people.'" "<b>Third occurrence</b><br>How beautiful are your sandals. When you walk to your land." "חמוקי ירכיך. Like the shin upon the thigh of the legs, according to the commentators."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:51.040319416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}